# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Google Drive for Desktop staging directories.
#
# The project root is Drive-synced. Drive creates these INSIDE the synced folder
# while transferring, so they appear at the repository root, hold dozens of
# transient numbered blobs, and vanish again. They were untracked and NOT ignored
# until 2026-09-15, which meant they showed up in `git status` and were one
# `git add .` away from being committed.
#
# They also make "the working tree is clean" a moving target: a status check can
# be empty one minute and show thirty untracked files the next, purely because a
# sync started. Ignoring them keeps status meaningful.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.tmp.driveupload/
.tmp.drivedownload/

# Virtual environments
#
# NOTE: gitignoring these does not stop Drive syncing them. Drive does not read
# .gitignore. .venv/ is ~408 MB and .mypy_cache/ ~17 MB of churn being uploaded
# on every change. Excluding them is a Drive-side configuration decision, not a
# git one.
.venv/
venv/

# Python caches
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
build/
dist/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The project datacenter, ignored at the FOLDER level.
#
# artifacts/ holds governance records, conversation transcripts, task packets,
# breadcrumbs, solver runs, imported inputs and generated outputs. None of it is
# tracked, so none of it exists in a clone. That is why nothing under artifacts/
# may be cited as evidence by a commit, and why a commit touching it is never
# self-contained or reproducible for anyone else.
#
# There is deliberately NO negation for anything inside it.
#
# The previous version of this file carried
#
#     !artifacts/.gitkeep
#
# with no preceding ignore rule for artifacts/ at all. A negation without a
# matching ignore pattern silently does nothing, so the folder was never actually
# ignored, and four generated files ended up tracked inside it -- the MIXED
# tracked/ignored state that then had to be unpicked by hand. Recorded here rather
# than quietly deleted, because the failure mode is invisible: git does not warn
# about a negation that matches nothing.
#
# Where the tracked counterparts live, both deliberately OUTSIDE this folder:
#   solver_inputs/   generated inputs the GUI solvers need (small, deterministic)
#   examples/        reference outputs, so a clone has something to compare against
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
artifacts/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Operator profiles: the folder exists in a clone, empty of designs.
#
# Chief Operator, 2026-09-15: "the profiles directory should clone empty and the
# profiles i work on should stay on disk and will be backed up to google drive but
# should not be pushed publicly."
#
# So spec-scope-profiles are the operator's working designs, not repository
# content. There is deliberately NO reference design shipped here, because there
# is no set design point -- MK0 was a planning baseline and will change with the
# design and the size.
#
# The MK0 profile the regression suite needs is therefore a TEST FIXTURE and lives
# at tests/data/mk0_benchtop_22kv.json, tracked. That separation is the point:
# "which design am I working on" and "what proves the physics has not drifted" are
# different questions and must not share a switch.
#
# Only README.md is tracked here, so the directory exists in a clone with an
# explanation in it rather than being absent or unexplained. The negation is safe
# because it is paired with the ignore rule directly above it -- verified with
# `git check-ignore -v`, per the .gitkeep incident recorded above.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
profiles/*
!profiles/README.md

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Machine-local external-tool locations.
#
# tools.local.json tells the detection layer where solvers live when they are not
# in a vendor default directory. It holds ABSOLUTE PATHS ON ONE MACHINE, so it is
# configuration rather than repository content and would be wrong in every clone.
#
# It exists because installing the tools on 2026-09-16 exposed a real gap:
# `configured-path` is the FIRST route in detect.ROUTE_ORDER and nothing in the
# suite could populate it. LTspice at B:\LTspice and QSPICE at B:\QSPICE were both
# working and both reported `tool-absent` -- correctly by the contract's own
# definition, since all four routes concluded, and wrongly in the only sense that
# matters. A working tool reported absent is exactly what the detection layer was
# built to prevent.
#
# A test asserts this rule holds, because a leaked config would publish one
# operator's directory layout.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
tools.local.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Solver exhaust inside solver_inputs/.
#
# solver_inputs/ is TRACKED, and a solver run writes its byproducts beside the
# input it was given. On 2026-09-18 the operator opened
# solver_inputs/ehd_llc_cw.cir directly in LTspice, which then wrote
# solver_inputs/ehd_llc_cw.log into the tracked directory. Caught immediately by
# tests/test_solver_inputs.py::test_every_tracked_solver_input_is_covered_by_this_module,
# which asserts every file on disk there is covered by a regeneration check -- a
# check written for drift that turned out to catch working-directory pollution too.
#
# These rules are belt-and-braces, NOT the fix. The fix is the discipline: copy a
# solver input to a scratch directory and run it there, so the tracked artifact
# whose SHA-256 a run record carries is never in the directory the tool is writing
# into. An ignore rule stops exhaust being staged; it does not stop the test
# failing, and it should not -- exhaust in solver_inputs/ means the discipline
# slipped, and that is worth being told about.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
solver_inputs/*.log
solver_inputs/*.raw
solver_inputs/*.op.raw
solver_inputs/*.net
solver_inputs/*.fail
solver_inputs/*.msh
